From 9e166bd3f422a2c341c1f028cdf66dd7d88d890e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 2 Sep 2026 10:19:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Run the tests under UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer, and stop on a
 report

The non-Release build already carries -fsanitize=address, and both CI
configurations build exactly that way (cmake . && make && make test, no
CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE), so the address sanitizer runs on every push. This adds
the undefined-behaviour one beside it.

-fno-sanitize-recover=undefined is the part that matters. Without it a
report is printed and the run continues, ctest still says PASSED, and the
suite reports green while it exercises undefined behaviour - which is
what it had been doing: the three defects fixed just before this commit
were all reachable from these five tests, and one of them, the shift by
35 in lshpack_dec_dec_int, is executed by a test case that has been in
test_int all along and expected -2 from it.

-fno-sanitize=alignment because deps/xxhash reads unaligned on purpose
and is compiled into every test and tool here; the alignment check
reports on that file and on nothing of ours. Every other check stays on,
including alignment's absence being the only exception.

Verified: 5/5 tests pass with this. Putting any one of the three defects
back turns the run red, which is the property being bought.
